-- coa13-ch3-preemption.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 3 (ss 560 to 577): allotment of equity
-- securities, existing shareholders' right of pre-emption. Lines 7716-7871 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of coa13-ch1-shares.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE "the text says no in its own words",
-- NOTHING "not covered"). A prohibition with an "unless" is asked as "is prohibited": JUST FALSE once the "unless" is met.
-- Every name begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 17, Chapter 3: Allotment of equity securities: existing shareholders' right of pre-emption`

§§ `Introductory (s 560)`

-- ---- s 560: Meaning of "equity securities" and related expressions --------------------------------------

-- src:7723 | “ordinary shares” means shares other than shares that as respects dividends and capital carry a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution.
@ref s 560(1) "ordinary shares" (src:7723)
GIVEN `the shares carry, as respects dividends, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares carry, as respects capital, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 560(1) the shares are ordinary shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares carry, as respects dividends, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution` AND `the shares carry, as respects capital, a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“ordinary shares” means shares other than shares that as respects dividends and capital carry a right to participate only up to a specified amount in a distribution"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:7720 | “equity securities” means—
-- src:7721 | (a) ordinary shares in the company, or
-- src:7722 | (b) rights to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares in the company;
@ref s 560(1) "equity securities" (src:7720-7722)
GIVEN `s 560(1) the shares are ordinary shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is a share in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a right to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 560(1) the thing is an equity security` MEANS
    IF `it is a right to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares in the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `it is a share in the company`
         THEN `s 560(1) the shares are ordinary shares`
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“equity securities” means— (a) ordinary shares in the company, or (b) rights to subscribe for, or to convert securities into, ordinary shares in the company"

-- src:7724 | (2) References in this Chapter to the allotment of equity securities—
-- src:7725 | (a) include the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any securities into, ordinary shares in the company, and
-- src:7726 | (b) do not include the allotment of shares pursuant to such a right.
@ref s 560(2) the allotment of equity securities includes the grant of a right, not the allotment of shares pursuant to it (src:7724-7726)
GIVEN `it is the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any securities into, ordinary shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the allotment of shares pursuant to such a right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 560(2) the transaction is an allotment of equity securities for the purposes of Chapter 3` MEANS
    IF `it is the allotment of shares pursuant to such a right`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Chapter to the allotment of equity securities ... (b) do not include the allotment of shares pursuant to such a right"
    ELSE IF `it is the grant of a right to subscribe for, or to convert any securities into, ordinary shares in the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the subsection lists what the allotment of equity securities includes and excludes and does not close the list

-- src:7727 | (3) References in this Chapter to the allotment of equity securities include the sale of ordinary shares in the company that immediately before the sale were held by the company as treasury shares.
@ref s 560(3) the allotment of equity securities includes a sale of ordinary shares held as treasury shares (src:7727)
GIVEN `it is the sale of ordinary shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares were held by the company as treasury shares immediately before the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 560(3) the sale is an allotment of equity securities for the purposes of Chapter 3` MEANS
    IF `it is the sale of ordinary shares in the company` AND `the shares were held by the company as treasury shares immediately before the sale`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include the sale of ordinary shares in the company that immediately before the sale were held by the company as treasury shares" lists one inclusion and does not close the list

§§ `Existing shareholders' right of pre-emption (ss 561 to 563)`

-- ---- s 561: Existing shareholders' right of pre-emption --------------------------------------------------

-- src:7731 | (a) it has made an offer to each person who holds ordinary shares in the company to allot to him on the same or more favourable terms a proportion of those securities that is as nearly as practicable equal to the proportion in nominal value held by him of the ordinary share capital of the company, and
@ref s 561(1)(a) the offer must be to each holder of ordinary shares, on the same or more favourable terms, in proportion (src:7731)
GIVEN `the company has made an offer to each person who holds ordinary shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is to allot to him on the same or more favourable terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer is of a proportion of those securities as nearly as practicable equal to the proportion in nominal value held by him of the ordinary share capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1)(a) the company has made the offers required` MEANS
    IF     `the company has made an offer to each person who holds ordinary shares in the company`
       AND `the offer is to allot to him on the same or more favourable terms`
       AND `the offer is of a proportion of those securities as nearly as practicable equal to the proportion in nominal value held by him of the ordinary share capital of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless— (a) it has made an offer to each person who holds ordinary shares ..." (a limb of an "unless" that is not met)

@ref s 561(1)(a) the proportion of the securities to be offered to a holder (src:7731)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the ordinary shares held by the holder` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the ordinary share capital of the company, treasury shares disregarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 561(1)(a) the proportion of the securities to be offered to the holder` MEANS
    `the nominal value of the ordinary shares held by the holder` DIVIDED BY `the nominal value of the ordinary share capital of the company, treasury shares disregarded`

@ref s 561(1)(a) the number of securities to be offered to a holder (src:7731)
GIVEN `the number of the equity securities to be allotted` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the ordinary shares held by the holder` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the ordinary share capital of the company, treasury shares disregarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 561(1)(a) the number of the equity securities to be offered to the holder` MEANS
    `the number of the equity securities to be allotted`
    TIMES (`s 561(1)(a) the proportion of the securities to be offered to the holder` `the nominal value of the ordinary shares held by the holder` `the nominal value of the ordinary share capital of the company, treasury shares disregarded`)

-- src:7732 | (b) the period during which any such offer may be accepted has expired or the company has received notice of the acceptance or refusal of every offer so made.
@ref s 561(1)(b) the offer period must have expired, or every offer accepted or refused (src:7732)
GIVEN `the period during which any such offer may be accepted has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has received notice of the acceptance or refusal of every offer so made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1)(b) the period has expired or every offer has been accepted or refused` MEANS
    IF `the period during which any such offer may be accepted has expired` OR `the company has received notice of the acceptance or refusal of every offer so made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless ... (b) the period during which any such offer may be accepted has expired or the company has received notice of the acceptance or refusal of every offer so made" (a limb of an "unless" that is not met)

-- src:7735 | (4) Shares held by the company as treasury shares are disregarded for the purposes of this section, so that—
-- src:7736 | (a) the company is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares, and
-- src:7737 | (b) the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital of the company.
@ref s 561(4) shares held as treasury shares are disregarded (src:7735-7737)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(4) the shares are disregarded for the purposes of section 561` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Shares held by the company as treasury shares are disregarded"

@ref s 561(4)(a) the company is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares (src:7736)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(4)(a) the company is treated as a person who holds ordinary shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of shares held by the company as treasury shares

@ref s 561(4)(b) the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital (src:7737)
GIVEN `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(4)(b) the shares are treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital` MEANS
    IF `the shares are held by the company as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of shares held by the company as treasury shares

-- src:7733 | (2) Securities that a company has offered to allot to a holder of ordinary shares may be allotted to him, or anyone in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment, without contravening subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 561(2) securities offered may be allotted to the holder or his renouncee without contravening (1)(b) (src:7733)
GIVEN `the securities were offered to the holder of ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allotment is to the holder, or to a person in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(2) the allotment contravenes section 561(1)(b)` MEANS
    IF `the securities were offered to the holder of ordinary shares` AND `the allotment is to the holder, or to a person in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be allotted to him, or anyone in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment, without contravening subsection (1)(b)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of securities offered to a holder and allotted to him or his renouncee

DECLARE `s 561(5) the sections to which section 561 is subject` HAS
    `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 564` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 565` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 567` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 568(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(c) the answer of sections 569 to 573` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 561(5)(d) the answer of section 576` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:7738 | (5) This section is subject to—
-- src:7739 | (a) sections 564 to 566A (exceptions to pre-emption right),
-- src:7740 | (b) sections 567 and 568 (exclusion of rights of pre-emption),
-- src:7741 | (c) sections 569 to 573 (disapplication of pre-emption rights), and
-- src:7742 | (d) section 576 (saving for certain older pre-emption procedures).
@ref s 561(5) section 561 is subject to ss 564-566A, 567-568, 569-573 and 576 (src:7738-7742)
GIVEN `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject` IS A `s 561(5) the sections to which section 561 is subject`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(5) section 561 is displaced by one of the sections to which it is subject` MEANS
    IF     `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 564` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 565` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(a) the answer of section 566A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 567` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(b) the answer of section 568(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(c) the answer of sections 569 to 573` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the answers of the sections to which section 561 is subject`'s `s 561(5)(d) the answer of section 576` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This section is subject to" lists sections and does not say "only"; none of them is shown to displace section 561

-- src:7730 | (1) A company must not allot equity securities to a person on any terms unless—
@ref s 561(1) a company must not allot equity securities to a person unless it has made the offers and the period has expired (src:7730)
GIVEN `the company allots, or proposes to allot, equity securities to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 561(1)(a) the company has made the offers required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 561(1)(b) the period has expired or every offer has been accepted or refused` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 561(5) section 561 is displaced by one of the sections to which it is subject` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 561(1) the company is prohibited from allotting the equity securities to the person` MEANS
    IF `the company allots, or proposes to allot, equity securities to a person`
    THEN IF `s 561(5) section 561 is displaced by one of the sections to which it is subject` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section is subject to" the exceptions, exclusions and disapplications (one is met)
         ELSE IF `s 561(1)(a) the company has made the offers required` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 561(1)(b) the period has expired or every offer has been accepted or refused` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not allot equity securities to a person on any terms unless" (the "unless" is met)
              ELSE IF `s 561(1)(a) the company has made the offers required` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 561(1)(b) the period has expired or every offer has been accepted or refused` EQUALS JUST FALSE
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb's answer is not known
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company must not allot equity securities to a person on any terms"

-- ---- s 562: Communication of pre-emption offers to shareholders ------------------------------------------

-- src:7745 | (2) The offer may be made in hard copy or electronic form.
@ref s 562(2) the offer may be made in hard copy or electronic form (src:7745)
GIVEN `the form in which the offer is made` IS A `Form of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(2) the offer may be made in this form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form in which the offer is made`
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:7746 | (3) If the holder—
-- src:7747 | (a) has no registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State and has not given to the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for the service of notices on him, or
-- src:7748 | (b) is the holder of a share warrant,
-- src:7749 | the offer may be made by causing it, or a notice specifying where a copy of it can be obtained or inspected, to be published in the Gazette.
@ref s 562(3) the offer may be made by publication in the Gazette if the holder has no address in the UK or an EEA State or holds a share warrant (src:7746-7749)
GIVEN `the holder has a registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has given the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for the service of notices on him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is the holder of a share warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(3) the offer may be made by causing it, or a notice of where it can be obtained, to be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF     (    (NOT (`the holder has a registered address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State`))
            AND (NOT (`the holder has given the company an address in the United Kingdom or an EEA State for the service of notices on him`)))
        OR `the holder is the holder of a share warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the holder (a) has no registered address ... and has not given ... or (b) is the holder of a share warrant" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- src:7750 | (4) The offer must state a period during which it may be accepted and the offer shall not be withdrawn before the end of that period.
@ref s 562(4) the offer must state a period during which it may be accepted (src:7750)
GIVEN `the offer states a period during which it may be accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(4) the offer meets the requirement to state a period` MEANS
    IF `the offer states a period during which it may be accepted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offer must state a period during which it may be accepted" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

@ref s 562(4) the offer shall not be withdrawn before the end of that period (src:7750)
GIVEN `the last day of the period during which the offer may be accepted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the offer is withdrawn` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(4) the offer may be withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the offer is withdrawn` AT MOST `the last day of the period during which the offer may be accepted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the offer shall not be withdrawn before the end of that period" (a withdrawal on the last day of the period is before its end: fork F-562(4))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition runs only until the end of that period

DECLARE `s 562(5) way the offer is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 562(5)(a) in hard copy form`
    `s 562(5)(b) in electronic form`
    `s 562(5)(c) by publication in the Gazette`

-- src:7751 | (5) The period must be a period of at least 14 days beginning—
-- src:7752 | (a) in the case of an offer made in hard copy form, with the date on which the offer is sent or supplied;
-- src:7753 | (b) in the case of an offer made in electronic form, with the date on which the offer is sent;
-- src:7754 | (c) in the case of an offer made by publication in the Gazette, with the date of publication.
@ref s 562(5) the period must be at least 14 days beginning with the date the offer is sent, supplied or published (src:7751-7754)
GIVEN `the way the offer is made` IS A `s 562(5) way the offer is made`
      `the date on which the offer is sent or supplied (hard copy), sent (electronic form), or published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period during which the offer may be accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 562(5) the period meets the requirement of at least 14 days` MEANS
    -- the period begins with the date in each of (a), (b) and (c), so its first day is that date and 14 days end 13 days later (fork F-562(5))
    IF `the last day of the period during which the offer may be accepted` AT LEAST (`the date on which the offer is sent or supplied (hard copy), sent (electronic form), or published in the Gazette` PLUS 13)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period must be a period of at least 14 days beginning— (a) ... with the date on which the offer is sent or supplied; (b) ... with the date on which the offer is sent; (c) ... with the date of publication" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- ---- s 563: Liability of company and officers in case of contravention -----------------------------------

-- src:7760 | (1) This section applies where there is a contravention of—
-- src:7761 | section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption), or
-- src:7762 | section 562 (communication of pre-emption offers to shareholders).
-- src:7763 | (2) The company and every officer of it who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention are jointly and severally liable to compensate any person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions for any loss, damage, costs or expenses which the person has sustained or incurred by reason of the contravention.
@ref s 563(2) the company and every officer who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention are jointly and severally liable to compensate (src:7760-7763)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 563(2) the company is liable to compensate the person` MEANS
    IF `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` AND `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to compensate any person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions" where there is a contravention

@ref s 563(2) the officer who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention is jointly and severally liable (src:7763)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 563(2) the officer is liable, jointly and severally with the company, to compensate the person` MEANS
    IF     `there is a contravention of section 561 or section 562`
       AND `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made in accordance with those provisions`
       AND `the officer knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of it who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention"

@ref s 563(2) the amount to be compensated (src:7763)
GIVEN `the loss, damage, costs or expenses the person has sustained or incurred by reason of the contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 563(2) the amount for which the company and the officers are jointly and severally liable` MEANS
    `the loss, damage, costs or expenses the person has sustained or incurred by reason of the contravention`

-- src:7764 | (3) No proceedings to recover any such loss, damage, costs or expenses shall be commenced after the expiration of two years—
-- src:7765 | (a) from the delivery to the registrar of companies of the return of allotment, or
-- src:7766 | (b) where equity securities other than shares are granted, from the date of the grant.
@ref s 563(3) no proceedings to recover after two years from delivery of the return, or from the grant (src:7764-7766)
GIVEN `the equity securities other than shares are granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar of companies` IS A DATE
      `the date of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 563(3) proceedings to recover the loss may be commenced` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` GREATER THAN `two years from the starting date`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings to recover any such loss, damage, costs or expenses shall be commenced after the expiration of two years"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars proceedings after two years and does not grant a right to commence them within it
    WHERE
        `the starting date` MEANS
            IF `the equity securities other than shares are granted`
            THEN `the date of the grant`
            ELSE `the date on which the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar of companies`
        `two years from the starting date` MEANS `add years` `the starting date` 2

§§ `Exceptions to right of pre-emption (ss 564 to 566A)`

-- src:7769 | Section 561(1) (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption) does not apply in relation to the allotment of bonus shares.
@ref s 564 section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares (src:7769)
GIVEN `the allotment is of bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 564 section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares` MEANS
    IF `the allotment is of bonus shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply in relation to the allotment of bonus shares"

-- src:7771 | Section 561(1) (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption) does not apply to a particular allotment of equity securities if these are, or are to be, wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash.
@ref s 565 section 561(1) does not apply if the securities are wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash (src:7771)
GIVEN `the equity securities are, or are to be, wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 565 section 561(1) does not apply to the allotment for non-cash consideration` MEANS
    IF `the equity securities are, or are to be, wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply to a particular allotment of equity securities if these are, or are to be, wholly or partly paid up otherwise than in cash" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:7773 | Section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption) does not apply to the allotment of equity securities that would, apart from any renunciation or assignment of the right to their allotment, be held under or allotted or transferred pursuant to an employees' share scheme.
@ref s 566 section 561 does not apply to equity securities held or allotted under an employees' share scheme (src:7773)
GIVEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the equity securities would, apart from any renunciation or assignment of the right to their allotment, be held under or allotted or transferred pursuant to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 566 section 561 does not apply to the allotment under an employees' share scheme` MEANS
    IF `the equity securities would, apart from any renunciation or assignment of the right to their allotment, be held under or allotted or transferred pursuant to the scheme`
    THEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` -- JUST TRUE: within the section; JUST FALSE is s 1166's no; NOTHING (points outside the text) passes through
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to the allotment of equity securities that would ... be held under or allotted or transferred pursuant to an employees' share scheme"

-- src:7775 | Section 561(1) (existing shareholders’ right of pre-emption) does not apply to an allotment of equity securities that is carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty).
@ref s 566A section 561(1) does not apply to an allotment carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement under Part 26A (src:7775)
GIVEN `the allotment is carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 26A the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
