    IF `the allotment is carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement`
    THEN `Part 26A the compromise or arrangement is sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to an allotment of equity securities that is carried out as part of a compromise or arrangement sanctioned in accordance with Part 26A"

§§ `Exclusion of right of pre-emption (ss 567 and 568)`

-- src:7778 | (1) All or any of the requirements of—
-- src:7779 | (a) section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption), or
-- src:7780 | (b) section 562 (communication of pre-emption offers to shareholders)
-- src:7781 | may be excluded by provision contained in the articles of a private company.
@ref s 567(1) the requirements of s 561 or s 562 may be excluded by provision in the articles of a private company (src:7778-7781)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is that of section 561 or of section 562` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exclusion is by provision contained in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 567(1) the requirements may be excluded` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `the requirement is that of section 561 or of section 562` AND `the exclusion is by provision contained in the articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be excluded by provision contained in the articles of a private company"

-- src:7782 | (2) They may be excluded—
-- src:7783 | (a) generally in relation to the allotment by the company of equity securities, or
-- src:7784 | (b) in relation to allotments of a particular description.
@ref s 567(2) the requirements may be excluded generally or for allotments of a particular description (src:7782-7784)
GIVEN `the exclusion is generally in relation to the allotment by the company of equity securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exclusion is in relation to allotments of a particular description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 567(2) the requirements may be excluded to this extent` MEANS
    IF `the exclusion is generally in relation to the allotment by the company of equity securities` OR `the exclusion is in relation to allotments of a particular description`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "They may be excluded (a) generally ... or (b) in relation to allotments of a particular description"

-- src:7786 | (4) A provision to which section 568 applies (exclusion of pre-emption right: corresponding right conferred by articles) is not to be treated as inconsistent with section 561.
@ref s 567(4) a provision to which s 568 applies is not treated as inconsistent with s 561 (src:7786)
GIVEN `section 568 applies to the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 567(4) the provision is treated as inconsistent with section 561` MEANS
    IF `section 568 applies to the provision`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A provision to which section 568 applies ... is not to be treated as inconsistent with section 561"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a provision to which section 568 applies

-- src:7785 | (3) Any requirement or authorisation contained in the articles of a private company that is inconsistent with either of those sections is treated for the purposes of this section as a provision excluding that section.
@ref s 567(3) an inconsistent requirement or authorisation in a private company's articles is treated as a provision excluding the section (src:7785)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement or authorisation is contained in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with section 561` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is inconsistent with section 562` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 567(4) the provision is treated as inconsistent with section 561` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 567(3) the requirement or authorisation is treated as a provision excluding the section` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `the requirement or authorisation is contained in the articles`
    THEN IF     (`it is inconsistent with section 561` AND (NOT (`s 567(4) the provision is treated as inconsistent with section 561` EQUALS JUST FALSE)))
             OR `it is inconsistent with section 562`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is inconsistent with either of those sections"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "contained in the articles of a private company"

-- src:7788 | (1) The provisions of this section apply where, in a case in which section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption) would otherwise apply—
-- src:7789 | (a) a company's articles contain provision (“pre-emption provision”) prohibiting the company from allotting ordinary shares of a particular class unless it has complied with the condition that it makes such an offer as is described in section 561(1) to each person who holds ordinary shares of that class, and
-- src:7790 | (b) in accordance with that provision—
-- src:7791 | (i) the company makes an offer to allot shares to such a holder, and
-- src:7792 | (ii) he or anyone in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment accepts the offer.
@ref s 568(1) the provisions of the section apply where the articles contain a pre-emption provision and the offer is made and accepted in accordance with it (src:7788-7792)
GIVEN `section 561 would otherwise apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles contain a pre-emption provision prohibiting the company from allotting ordinary shares of a particular class unless it has made such an offer as is described in section 561(1) to each person who holds ordinary shares of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with that provision the company makes an offer to allot shares to such a holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder, or anyone in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment, accepts the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(1) the provisions of section 568 apply` MEANS
    IF     `section 561 would otherwise apply`
       AND `the articles contain a pre-emption provision prohibiting the company from allotting ordinary shares of a particular class unless it has made such an offer as is described in section 561(1) to each person who holds ordinary shares of that class`
       AND `in accordance with that provision the company makes an offer to allot shares to such a holder`
       AND `the holder, or anyone in whose favour he has renounced his right to their allotment, accepts the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this section apply where, in a case in which section 561 would otherwise apply— (a) ... and (b) ..." (a "where" that fails)

-- src:7793 | (2) In that case, section 561 does not apply to the allotment of those shares and the company may allot them accordingly.
@ref s 568(2) section 561 does not apply to the allotment of those shares and the company may allot them (src:7793)
GIVEN `s 568(1) the provisions of section 568 apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(2) section 561 does not apply to the allotment because the articles confer a corresponding right` MEANS
    `s 568(1) the provisions of section 568 apply` -- "In that case": JUST TRUE is the case; JUST FALSE is the "where" of subsection (1) failing; NOTHING passes through

-- src:7794 | (3) The provisions of section 562 (communication of pre-emption offers to shareholders) apply in relation to offers made in pursuance of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles.
-- src:7795 | This is subject to section 567 (exclusion of requirements by private companies).
@ref s 568(3) section 562 applies to offers made in pursuance of the pre-emption provision, subject to s 567 (src:7794-7795)
GIVEN `the offer is made in pursuance of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 567 the requirement of section 562 is excluded by the articles of a private company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(3) section 562 applies to the offer` MEANS
    IF `the offer is made in pursuance of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles`
    THEN IF `s 567 the requirement of section 562 is excluded by the articles of a private company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to section 567 (exclusion of requirements by private companies)" (the exception is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to offers made in pursuance of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles"

-- src:7796 | (4) If there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles, the company, and every officer of it who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention, are jointly and severally liable to compensate any person to whom an offer should have been made under the provision for any loss, damage, costs or expenses which the person has sustained or incurred by reason of the contravention.
@ref s 568(4) the company and every officer who knowingly authorised or permitted a contravention of the articles' pre-emption provision are jointly and severally liable (src:7796)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(4) the company is liable to compensate the person` MEANS
    IF `there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles` AND `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made under the provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles" (the liability is stated for that case only)

@ref s 568(4) the officer who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention is jointly and severally liable (src:7796)
GIVEN `there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(4) the officer is liable, jointly and severally with the company, to compensate the person` MEANS
    IF     `there is a contravention of the pre-emption provision of the company's articles`
       AND `the person is a person to whom an offer should have been made under the provision`
       AND `the officer knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of it who knowingly authorised or permitted the contravention"

-- src:7797 | (5) No proceedings to recover any such loss, damage, costs or expenses may be commenced after the expiration of two years—
-- src:7798 | (a) from the delivery to the registrar of companies of the return of allotment, or
-- src:7799 | (b) where equity securities other than shares are granted, from the date of the grant.
@ref s 568(5) no proceedings to recover after two years from delivery of the return, or from the grant (src:7797-7799)
GIVEN `the equity securities other than shares are granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar of companies` IS A DATE
      `the date of the grant` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 568(5) proceedings to recover the loss may be commenced` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the proceedings are commenced` GREATER THAN `two years from the starting date`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings to recover any such loss, damage, costs or expenses may be commenced after the expiration of two years"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars proceedings after two years and does not grant a right to commence them within it
    WHERE
        `the starting date` MEANS
            IF `the equity securities other than shares are granted`
            THEN `the date of the grant`
            ELSE `the date on which the return of allotment was delivered to the registrar of companies`
        `two years from the starting date` MEANS `add years` `the starting date` 2

§§ `Disapplication of pre-emption rights (ss 569 to 573)`

-- src:7802 | (1) The directors of a private company that has only one class of shares may be given power by the articles, or by a special resolution of the company, to allot equity securities of that class as if section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption)—
