    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must make a written statement setting out (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..." (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7833 | (7) The directors' statement must—
-- src:7834 | (a) if the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, be sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:7835 | (b) if the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, be circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice.
@ref s 571(7) the directors' statement must be sent or submitted with a written resolution, or circulated with the notice of a general meeting (src:7833-7835)
GIVEN `the way the resolution is proposed` IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the statement was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement was circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way the resolution is proposed`
    WHEN `as a written resolution` THEN
        IF `the statement was sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted to him`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors' statement must— (a) if the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, be sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
    WHEN `at a meeting on a show of hands` THEN
        IF `the statement was circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, be circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)
    WHEN `at a meeting on a poll` THEN
        IF `the statement was circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, be circulated to the members entitled to notice of the meeting with that notice" (a bare "must" not done: a fork line)

-- src:7826 | (5) A special resolution under this section, or a special resolution to renew such a resolution, must not be proposed unless—
-- src:7827 | (a) it is recommended by the directors, and
-- src:7828 | (b) the directors have complied with the following provisions.
@ref s 571(5) a special resolution under the section, or to renew one, must not be proposed unless the directors recommend it and have complied (src:7826-7828)
GIVEN `the special resolution is recommended by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 571(6) the directors have made the written statement required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 571(5) the proposal of the special resolution is barred` MEANS
    IF     `the special resolution is recommended by the directors`
       AND `s 571(6) the directors have made the written statement required` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be proposed unless— (a) it is recommended by the directors, and (b) the directors have complied with the following provisions" (the "unless" is met)
    ELSE IF     (NOT (`the special resolution is recommended by the directors`))
             OR `s 571(6) the directors have made the written statement required` EQUALS JUST FALSE
             OR `s 571(7) the directors' statement has been sent, submitted or circulated as required` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb's answer is not known

-- src:7837 | (1) This section applies in relation to a directors' statement under section 571 (special resolution disapplying pre-emption rights) that is sent, submitted or circulated under subsection (7) of that section.
-- src:7838 | (2) A person who knowingly or recklessly authorises or permits the inclusion of any matter that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular in such a statement commits an offence.
@ref s 572(2) offence: knowingly or recklessly authorising or permitting a misleading, false or deceptive matter in the statement (src:7837-7838)
GIVEN `the statement is a directors' statement under section 571 that is sent, submitted or circulated under subsection (7) of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly or recklessly authorises or permits the inclusion of a matter in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 572(2) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF     `the statement is a directors' statement under section 571 that is sent, submitted or circulated under subsection (7) of that section`
       AND `the person knowingly or recklessly authorises or permits the inclusion of a matter in it`
       AND `the matter is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who knowingly or recklessly authorises or permits the inclusion of any matter that is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular in such a statement commits an offence"

-- src:7839 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7840 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:7841 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:7842 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:7843 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 572(3)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment: imprisonment not exceeding two years or a fine, or both (src:7839-7843)
`s 572(3)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 2, unit IS Years)
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE

@ref s 572(3)(b)(i) penalty on summary conviction in England and Wales: imprisonment not exceeding twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or both (src:7842)
`s 572(3)(b)(i) penalty on summary conviction in England and Wales` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 12, unit IS Months)
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE

@ref s 572(3)(b)(ii) penalty on summary conviction in Scotland: imprisonment not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or both (src:7843)
`s 572(3)(b)(ii) penalty on summary conviction in Scotland` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE

@ref s 572(3)(b)(ii) the same penalty on summary conviction in Northern Ireland (src:7843)
`s 572(3)(b)(ii) penalty on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period WITH `number of units` IS 6, unit IS Months)
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE

@ref s 572(3) a person guilty of an offence under s 572 is liable (src:7839-7843)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 572(3) the penalties for an offence under section 572` MEANS
    LIST `s 572(3)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`
       , `s 572(3)(b)(i) penalty on summary conviction in England and Wales`
       , `s 572(3)(b)(ii) penalty on summary conviction in Scotland`
       , `s 572(3)(b)(ii) penalty on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`

-- src:7845 | (1) This section applies in relation to a sale of shares that is an allotment of equity securities by virtue of section 560(3)(sale of shares held by company as treasury shares).
@ref s 573(1) the section applies to a sale of shares that is an allotment of equity securities by virtue of s 560(3) (src:7845)
GIVEN `s 560(3) the sale is an allotment of equity securities for the purposes of Chapter 3` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` MEANS
    `s 560(3) the sale is an allotment of equity securities for the purposes of Chapter 3` -- JUST TRUE: the section applies; NOTHING (includes) passes through, since section 560(3) does not close its list

-- src:7846 | (2) The directors of a company may be given power by the articles, or by a special resolution of the company, to allot equity securities as if section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption)—
-- src:7847 | (a) did not apply to the allotment, or
-- src:7848 | (b) applied to the allotment with such modifications as the directors may determine.
@ref s 573(2) the directors may be given power by the articles or a special resolution to allot as if s 561 did not apply or applied modified (src:7846-7848)
GIVEN `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the power is given by the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution giving the power is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(2) the directors may be given the power to allot equity securities as if section 561 did not apply or applied with modifications` MEANS
    IF `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the power is given by the articles` OR `s 283 the resolution giving the power is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be given power by the articles, or by a special resolution of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in relation to a sale of shares that is an allotment of equity securities by virtue of section 560(3)"

-- src:7849 | (3) The provisions of section 570(2) and (4) apply in that case as they apply to a case within subsection (1) of that section.
@ref s 573(3) the provisions of s 570(2) and (4) apply in that case (src:7849)
GIVEN `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(3) section 570(2) and (4) apply to the case` MEANS
    IF `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in that case as they apply to a case within subsection (1) of that section"

-- src:7850 | (4) The company may by special resolution resolve that section 561—
-- src:7851 | (a) shall not apply to a specified allotment of securities, or
-- src:7852 | (b) shall apply to the allotment with such modifications as may be specified in the resolution.
@ref s 573(4) the company may by special resolution resolve that s 561 shall not apply to a specified allotment or shall apply modified (src:7850-7852)
GIVEN `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(4) the company may by special resolution resolve that section 561 shall not apply or shall apply with modifications` MEANS
    IF `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company may by special resolution resolve" in a case to which the section applies

-- src:7853 | (5) The provisions of section 571(2) and (4) to (7) apply in that case as they apply to a case within subsection (1) of that section.
@ref s 573(5) the provisions of s 571(2) and (4) to (7) apply in that case (src:7853)
GIVEN `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 573(5) section 571(2) and (4) to (7) apply to the case` MEANS
    IF `s 573(1) section 573 applies to the sale` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in that case as they apply to a case within subsection (1) of that section"

§§ `Supplementary (ss 574 to 577)`

-- src:7856 | (1) In this Chapter, in relation to an offer to allot securities required by—
-- src:7857 | (a) section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption), or
-- src:7858 | (b) any provision to which section 568 applies (articles conferring corresponding right),
-- src:7859 | a reference (however expressed) to the holder of shares of any description is to whoever was the holder of shares of that description at the close of business on a date to be specified in the offer.
@ref s 574(1) the holder of shares for the purposes of an offer is whoever held them at the close of business on the date specified in the offer (src:7856-7859)
GIVEN `the person was the holder of shares of that description at the close of business on the date specified in the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(1) the person is the holder of shares of that description in relation to the offer` MEANS
    IF `the person was the holder of shares of that description at the close of business on the date specified in the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference (however expressed) to the holder of shares of any description is to whoever was the holder of shares of that description at the close of business on a date to be specified in the offer"

-- src:7860 | (2) The specified date must fall within the period of 28 days immediately before the date of the offer.
@ref s 574(2) the specified date must fall within the 28 days immediately before the date of the offer (src:7860)
GIVEN `the date specified in the offer` IS A DATE
      `the date of the offer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 574(2) the specified date falls within the period of 28 days immediately before the date of the offer` MEANS
    IF `the date specified in the offer` AT LEAST (`the date of the offer` MINUS 28) AND `the date specified in the offer` AT MOST (`the date of the offer` MINUS 1)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The specified date must fall within the period of 28 days immediately before the date of the offer" (a period fixed in its own words; the date of the offer itself is not in the period: fork F-574(2))

-- src:7862 | (1) The provisions of this Chapter are without prejudice to any other enactment by virtue of which a company is prohibited (whether generally or in specified circumstances) from offering or allotting equity securities to any person.
@ref s 575(1) the provisions of the Chapter are without prejudice to another enactment's prohibition on offering or allotting equity securities (src:7862)
GIVEN `another enactment prohibits the company, generally or in specified circumstances, from offering or allotting equity securities to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 575(1) the provisions of Chapter 3 affect the other enactment's prohibition` MEANS
    IF `another enactment prohibits the company, generally or in specified circumstances, from offering or allotting equity securities to the person`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The provisions of this Chapter are without prejudice to any other enactment by virtue of which a company is prohibited"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of an enactment that prohibits offering or allotting

-- src:7863 | (2) Where a company cannot by virtue of such an enactment offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company, those shares are disregarded for the purposes of section 561 (existing shareholders' right of pre-emption), so that—
-- src:7864 | (a) the person is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares, and
-- src:7865 | (b) the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital of the company.
@ref s 575(2) where an enactment bars the company from offering or allotting to a holder, those shares are disregarded for s 561 (src:7863-7865)
GIVEN `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 575(2) the shares are disregarded for the purposes of section 561` MEANS
    IF `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company cannot by virtue of such an enactment offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company, those shares are disregarded" (a "where" that fails)

@ref s 575(2)(a) the person is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares (src:7864)
GIVEN `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 575(2)(a) the person is treated as a person who holds ordinary shares` MEANS
    IF `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person is not treated as a person who holds ordinary shares"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of a company that cannot offer or allot to the person by virtue of an enactment

@ref s 575(2)(b) the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital (src:7865)
GIVEN `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 575(2)(b) the shares are treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital` MEANS
    IF `the company cannot, by virtue of such an enactment, offer or allot equity securities to a holder of ordinary shares of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the shares are not treated as forming part of the ordinary share capital of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of a company that cannot offer or allot to the holder by virtue of an enactment

-- src:7867 | (1) In the case of a public company the provisions of this Chapter do not apply to an allotment of equity securities that are subject to a pre-emption requirement in relation to which section 96(1) of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) or Article 106(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) applied immediately before the commencement of this Chapter.
@ref s 576(1) the Chapter does not apply to equity securities subject to an older pre-emption requirement, in a public company (src:7867)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the equity securities are subject to a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of Chapter 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(1) the provisions of Chapter 3 do not apply to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the equity securities are subject to a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(1) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(1) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of Chapter 3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a public company the provisions of this Chapter do not apply to an allotment of equity securities that are subject to a pre-emption requirement"

-- src:7868 | (2) In the case of a private company a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(3) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(3) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of this Chapter shall have effect, so long as the company remains a private company, as if it were contained in the company's articles.
@ref s 576(2) in a private company an older s 96(3) requirement has effect as if in the articles so long as the company remains private (src:7868)
GIVEN `s 4(1) the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company remains a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(3) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(3) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of Chapter 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(2) the requirement has effect as if it were contained in the company's articles` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) the company is a private company` AND `there is a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(3) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(3) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of Chapter 3`
    THEN IF `the company remains a private company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall have effect, so long as the company remains a private company, as if it were contained in the company's articles"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a private company a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(3) ... applied immediately before the commencement of this Chapter"

-- src:7869 | (3) A pre-emption requirement to which section 96(4) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(4) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of this section shall be treated for the purposes of this Chapter as if it were contained in the company's articles.
@ref s 576(3) an older s 96(4) requirement is treated as if contained in the articles (src:7869)
GIVEN `there is a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(4) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(4) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 576(3) the requirement is treated as if it were contained in the company's articles` MEANS
    IF `there is a pre-emption requirement to which section 96(4) of the Companies Act 1985 or Article 106(4) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 applied immediately before the commencement of the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A pre-emption requirement to which section 96(4) ... applied immediately before the commencement of this section"

